# Keep LF line endings in every checkout, including on Windows, whatever the client's
# core.autocrlf (Git for Windows sets it true system-wide): a CRLF .sh script fails under
# WSL with "$'\r': command not found". Git still leaves binary files alone. Above the LFS
# rule, which it must not override: later lines win, so cpi.db stays binary and in LFS.
* text=auto eol=lf
cpi.db filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
